eeg|v|That which hinders or impedes motion; hence, an encumbrance, restraint, or impediment, of any kind. ; A weight, as a log or block of wood, attached to a man or an animal to hinder motion. ; A shoe, or sandal, intended to protect the feet from wet, or to increase the apparent stature, and having, therefore, a very thick sole. Cf. Chopine. ; To encumber or load, especially with something that impedes motion; to hamper. ; To obstruct so as to hinder motion in or through; to choke up; as, to clog a tube or a channel. ; To burden; to trammel; to embarrass; to perplex. ; To become clogged; to become loaded or encumbered, as with extraneous matter. ; To coalesce or adhere; to unite in a mass.	s:1lja,81,11;1hnj,70,17;u7p,45,4~1hnj,70,17;1lja,81,11;u7p,45,4	D:2dm8,8,3~2dm8,8,3
